WEBVTT

NOTE
PLACEHOLDER SIDECAR -- no film is attached to this pipeline yet.

Authored in-project for the Changeover demo rig. The caption TEXT below is
authored test content written for this project; it is not a transcript of
anything. The cue TIMING is a real, monotonic 2.002s-cadence timeline that a
producer can diff against an advancing program clock.

PROVENANCE CORRECTION: an earlier version of this file was named
tears_of_steel.en.vtt and stated the program feed was Tears of Steel
(c) Blender Foundation, CC BY 3.0. That attribution was WRONG. The file it
described (fixtures/source.mp4) was 1920x1080 / 179.2s, whereas Tears of Steel
is natively 1920x800 / ~12:14, and inspection showed it was not a film at all.
No open-license film has been part of this pipeline at any point. That source
file has been removed; this sidecar is retained as a working placeholder until
real films are supplied.

The cue timings here are film-independent: they are wall-clock offsets from
program start, not frame boundaries of any particular video. When a real film is
attached, either these timings work as-is against it or a per-film sidecar is
authored to the spec in README.md.

Cue cadence is deliberately ~2s with ~0.5s gaps so that a stalled cue producer
is measurable against the program clock within a few seconds.

